# Input

Input collects short text and numeric values with consistent labels, validation, supporting text, icons, and disabled states. Number inputs include minus and plus controls while preserving native spinbutton behavior.

Keep validation logic in the form and pass `error` only after the value should be considered invalid. See the API table for sizing, message placement, custom snippets, and layout options.

<DocsExample title="Input usage example" source={inputExampleSource} htmlSource={inputExampleHtmlSource}><InputExample /></DocsExample>

## Time input

Use the native `time` input for locale-aware time entry and platform picker behavior. Set `step` in seconds when the workflow uses fixed intervals.

<DocsExample title="Time input example" source={timeInputExampleSource} htmlSource={timeInputExampleHtmlSource}><TimeInputExample /></DocsExample>
